  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">YEMEN Floodings</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">One round of Multi Purpose Cash Transfer (MPCT) to 750 targeted Internally Displaced Person (IDP) households (550 HHs in Hajjah and 200 HHs in Marib)  Project team will conduct During Distribution Monitoring (DDM) on the same day of the distribution  Procure and distribute 500 basic hygiene kits and tarpaulins, of which 300 kits will include dignity kit for women and girls Procure and distribute 100 water tanks with size of 500 litre to affected IDP households  Construct 40 emergency latrines (40 in Marib) and rehabilitate 100 latrines (50 in Marib and 50 in Hajjah) to IDP whose latrines were destroyed or severely damaged.  Desludging of Communal Pit Latrines: At least 2,350 m3 with average of 100m3 per day of wastewater removal to safe disposal site is targeted along 3 months period; with total of 7,050 m3 Distribute chlorination and disinfection of water sources in Marib.  Public Health and Hygiene Promotion Support community alert system through Community health volunteer for referral of disease outbreaks Conducting Rapid protection assessment for the targeted IDPs camps in Marib effected by the flood to identify the existence protection risks, available services and access challenges.  Oxfam will conduct protection analysis in Marib in line with the centrality of protection approach Oxfam will provide protection cash assistance to support 100HHs/individuals in Marib and 20 HHs/individuals in Hajjah with protection risks  Regularly mapping of the available services and communicating relevant services providers to ensure effective referral pathway</narrative>
  </description>
